{
	"type": "root",
	"children": [
		{
			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: How to set up Playwright with Next.js\nnav_title: Playwright\ndescription: Learn how to set up Playwright with Next.js for End-to-End (E2E) Testing."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Playwright is a testing framework that lets you automate Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with a single API. You can use it to write "
				},
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "End-to-End (E2E)"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " testing. This guide will show you how to set up Playwright with Next.js and write your first tests."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Quickstart"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The fastest way to get started is to use "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "create-next-app"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " with the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://github.com/vercel/next.js/tree/canary/examples/with-playwright",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "with-playwright example"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". This will create a Next.js project complete with Playwright configured."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"pnpm\"",
			"value": "pnpm create next-app --example with-playwright with-playwright-app"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"npm\"",
			"value": "npx create-next-app@latest --example with-playwright with-playwright-app"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"yarn\"",
			"value": "yarn create next-app --example with-playwright with-playwright-app"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"bun\"",
			"value": "bun create next-app --example with-playwright with-playwright-app"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Manual setup"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "To install Playwright, run the following command:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"pnpm\"",
			"value": "pnpm create playwright"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"npm\"",
			"value": "npm init playwright"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"yarn\"",
			"value": "yarn create playwright"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "bash",
			"meta": "package=\"bun\"",
			"value": "bun create playwright"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "This will take you through a series of prompts to set up and configure Playwright for your project, including adding a "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "playwright.config.ts"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " file. Please refer to the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://playwright.dev/docs/intro#installation",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Playwright installation guide"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " for the step-by-step guide."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Creating your first Playwright E2E test"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Create two new Next.js pages:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "tsx",
			"meta": "filename=\"app/page.tsx\"",
			"value": "import Link from 'next/link'\n\nexport default function Page() {\n\treturn (\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<h1>Home</h1>\n\t\t\t<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link>\n\t\t</div>\n\t)\n}"
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "tsx",
			"meta": "filename=\"app/about/page.tsx\"",
			"value": "import Link from 'next/link'\n\nexport default function Page() {\n\treturn (\n\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<h1>About</h1>\n\t\t\t<Link href=\"/\">Home</Link>\n\t\t</div>\n\t)\n}"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Then, add a test to verify that your navigation is working correctly:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "ts",
			"meta": "filename=\"tests/example.spec.ts\"",
			"value": "import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test'\n\ntest('should navigate to the about page', async ({ page }) => {\n\t// Start from the index page (the baseURL is set via the webServer in the playwright.config.ts)\n\tawait page.goto('http://localhost:3000/')\n\t// Find an element with the text 'About' and click on it\n\tawait page.click('text=About')\n\t// The new URL should be \"/about\" (baseURL is used there)\n\tawait expect(page).toHaveURL('http://localhost:3000/about')\n\t// The new page should contain an h1 with \"About\"\n\tawait expect(page.locator('h1')).toContainText('About')\n})"
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": ": You can use "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "page.goto(\"/\")"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " instead of "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "page.goto(\"http://localhost:3000/\")"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": ", if you add "
						},
						{
							"type": "link",
							"title": null,
							"url": "https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-testoptions#test-options-base-url",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "\"baseURL\": \"http://localhost:3000\""
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " to the "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "playwright.config.ts"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " "
						},
						{
							"type": "link",
							"title": null,
							"url": "https://playwright.dev/docs/test-configuration",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "configuration file"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Testing instant navigations"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If you're using Cache Components, the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "instant()"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " helper from "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "@next/playwright"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " lets you assert what is visible immediately after a navigation, before any dynamic content streams in. See the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../instant-navigation.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Instant navigation guide"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../../03-api-reference/03-file-conventions/02-route-segment-config/instant.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "instant"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " API reference"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " for setup and examples."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Running your Playwright tests"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Playwright will simulate a user navigating your application using three browsers: Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, this requires your Next.js server to be running. We recommend running your tests against your production code to more closely resemble how your application will behave."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Run "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "npm run build"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "npm run start"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", then run "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "npx playwright test"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " in another terminal window to run the Playwright tests."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": ": Alternatively, you can use the "
						},
						{
							"type": "link",
							"title": null,
							"url": "https://playwright.dev/docs/test-webserver/",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "webServer"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " feature to let Playwright start the development server and wait until it's fully available."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Running Playwright on Continuous Integration (CI)"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Playwright will by default run your tests in the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://playwright.dev/docs/ci#running-headed",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "headless mode"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". To install all the Playwright dependencies, run "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "npx playwright install-deps"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "You can learn more about Playwright and Continuous Integration from these resources:"
				}
